  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Wednesday) \nIssued at 1040 AM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nThis weekend, a trough from the Rockies will move to the eastern \nstates. It will pull a cold front through our area Sunday and \nSunday night. Atmospheric moisture and instability looks lean, so\nare posting just a 20 to 40 percent chance for showers, and any\nrainfall will be light. Otherwise, a shot of cooler air will \nfollow the front for Monday and Tuesday. \n \nAfter Tuesday, model spread increases, giving us low confidence in\nthe details heading into Thanksgiving. Right now, the NBM shows \ncooler than normal temperatures and low, but not zero shower \nchances. Some of the ensemble members show a much more rainy \npattern in the region, mostly east of our coverage area. You will\nwant to keep up with the latest forecasts if your Thanksgiving \nplans include travel outside of Middle TN.",
